    "rationale": "The teach-back method is most effective as a short-term evaluation method is correct. This method involves the client explaining what they have learned in their own words or demonstrating a skill.\n\nThe teach-back method is better for return demonstration of a new skill is incorrect. The teach-back method is effective for both explaining and demonstrating what a client has learned.\n\nThe teach-back method might not be practical for long-term evaluation is correct. In some cases, the nurse might not interact one on one with the clients again, meaning that long-term evaluation using the teach-back method would be impractical.\n\nUsing the teach-back method allows the nurse to clarify misconceptions by the client is correct. When a client explains or demonstrates what they have learned, the nurse can use the teach-back method to catch any misconceptions or errors.\n\nThe client should recite what the nurse said during the session is incorrect. The client should explain what they have learned in their own words.",
