    "rationale": "\"Why did you wait so long to come to the clinic?\" is incorrect. The nurse should not ask for explanations from the client by using \"why\" questions, as they can cause resentment and mistrust. This is a nontherapeutic communication technique. \"How can I help you today?\" is correct. The nurse should be respectful when interacting with clients. This question is recommended by the Agency for Health Care Research and Quality to build cultural competency skills and is a form of therapeutic communication. \"In the future, you need to come in sooner when you get sick.\" is incorrect. The nurse should not use language that is aggressive or suggests disapproval of the client. This is a nontherapeutic communication technique. \"What seems to make your symptoms better?\" is correct. The nurse should be respectful when interacting with clients. This question is recommended by the Agency for Health Care Research and Quality to build cultural competency skills and is a form of therapeutic communication. \"What have you done about your problem?\" is correct. The nurse should be respectful when interacting with clients. This question is recommended by the Agency for Health Care Research and Quality to build cultural competency skills and is a form of therapeutic communication.",
